Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 22:02:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] F635-10: LOGIC_SKIP_KAMIKAZE_ON_DISCARDED_HIT (data
 16.635.3), upstream e5462c82 (#741) cherry-picked

A hit discarded for distance (target left the range during the wind-up) skips its end, where a
Kamikaze owner destroys itself, under the published global; the 16.402 tables publish none and the
hit always ends (crforge already ran hitEnded for a missed hit: the ticket premise that it returned
before the kill does not hold). Kamikaze rows in 16.635.3: BattleRam, ElectroSpirit, FireSpirits,
GoblinDemolisher_kamikaze_form, HealSpirit, IceSpirits(_EV1), SkeletonBalloon(_EV1), SuspiciousBush,
Wallbreaker(_EV1, _mini). Conflicts: Fidelity notes only (BattleWorld, WorldEntity).

Red: end not skipped, 1 of 22 BattleKamikazeDiscardedHitTest/HitApplication* fails on 16.635.3; green.
Core: 16.402.22 2157/0; 16.635.3 (guard bypassed for the run) 2157/0.

(cherry picked from commit e5462c8278f537a99361f248444efef53efebe1f)
